From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meiso Glass K230D integration <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] k230d-zero: select GC2093 and declare two-buffer vb2 minimum

The BPI CanMV K230D Zero used by this integration exposes a GC2093 sensor,
while its board defconfig currently selects IMX335. Select GC2093 so the
generated vvcam configuration matches the board.

The bundled ISP userspace requests a second capture buffer while handling
STREAMON. A one-buffer vb2 queue can therefore enter that path without the
buffer the userspace contract expects. Declare a driver minimum of two
buffers. Linux 6.6 vb2 raises the allocated REQBUFS count to this minimum and
does not start streaming until the minimum has been queued.

This is a bounded public-BSP guard, not a repair for synchronization inside
the closed-source ISP server. Camera consumers in this integration must still
request and queue at least four capture buffers; the two-buffer kernel minimum
only prevents the known single-buffer trigger.
---
 .../configs/BPI-CanMV-K230D-Zero_defconfig              | 2 +-
 .../package/vvcam/v4l2/video/vvcam_video_register.c     | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/buildroot-overlay/configs/BPI-CanMV-K230D-Zero_defconfig b/buildroot-overlay/configs/BPI-CanMV-K230D-Zero_defconfig
--- a/buildroot-overlay/configs/BPI-CanMV-K230D-Zero_defconfig
+++ b/buildroot-overlay/configs/BPI-CanMV-K230D-Zero_defconfig
@@ -30,3 +30,3 @@
 BR2_PACKAGE_VVCAM=y
-BR2_PACKAGE_VVCAM_DEF_SENSOR="imx335"
+BR2_PACKAGE_VVCAM_DEF_SENSOR="gc2093"
 BR2_PACKAGE_AUDIO_DEMO=y
diff --git a/buildroot-overlay/package/vvcam/v4l2/video/vvcam_video_register.c b/buildroot-overlay/package/vvcam/v4l2/video/vvcam_video_register.c
--- a/buildroot-overlay/package/vvcam/v4l2/video/vvcam_video_register.c
+++ b/buildroot-overlay/package/vvcam/v4l2/video/vvcam_video_register.c
@@ -1212,4 +1212,11 @@ static int vvcam_video_queue_init(struct vvcam_video_dev *vvcam_vdev)
     queue->buf_struct_size = sizeof(struct vvcam_vb2_buffer);
-	queue->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC;
+    queue->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC;
+    /*
+     * The bundled ISP userspace requests a second capture buffer while
+     * handling STREAMON. Let vb2 raise smaller REQBUFS requests and defer
+     * start_streaming until two buffers have been queued. Consumers still
+     * request and queue at least four buffers.
+     */
+    queue->min_buffers_needed = 2;
     queue->lock = &vvcam_vdev->video_lock;
     queue->dev = vvcam_vdev->vvcam_mdev->dev;

--
